    "md5": "148f861de75205f74c665a8704168606",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1856,
    "chunk_text": "It was he who acquired the land for the playground of the Beruwala Central College amidst many objections and also constructed the two new buildings of the Roman Catholic School near the Beruwala Police Station. The two main buildings of Warapitiya School, the meeting halls of Gnanissara and Aluthgamveediya Balika Vidyalayas, the building of the Pambe School and the prayer hall of the Hettimulla Temple, the Munghena Century School building and the two-storied Duwegoda School, the Walatara and Kalavila School buildings, the Meeting Halls of Al Hambra Vidyalay Naleem Hajiyar Girls\u2019 School and the two-storied building of the Roman Catholic School in Diyalagoda were among his achievements.\n\nIt was Mr. Bakeer Markar who proposed the inclusion of the areas of Beruwala, Aluthgama, Moragalla and Kaluwamodara in the Bentota Tourism Zone. It is no secret how the then Director General of the Tourism Board, Mr. Thahir, and a group of high-ranking officials of the Board opposed this decision by pointing out various negatives. But Mr. Bakeer Markar fought a lone battle to designate these areas within the tourist zone leading to the uplifting the economic conditions of the people of that area.\n\nThe people of Beruwala still remember how he took the initiative to establish several shopping complexes in his electorate with the involvement of the private sector. He also took the initiative to build a big shopping complex for the development of Aluthgama town, amidst the challenges faced in courts with regard to it. The Aluthgama Town Hall building was also built by him. The model village of Wellathuduwa, Aluthgama was built during his time. The Post Office buildings at Aluthgama and Beruwala (new), Maggona, Dhargatown, Halkadawila and the Beruwala and Payagala Telephone Exchange Centers were all built under the guidance of Mr. Bakeer Markar."
  },
