    "chunk_size_bytes": 1610,
    "chunk_text": "As vigils gather to remember the 40th anniversary of the Chernobyl disaster, the worst nuclear plant accident the world has known, another major policy decision should be applauded, this government\u2019s refusal of the nuclear power plant offer by Russia, heeding our local scientists who warn that the risks far outweigh the advantages.\n\nThis line of thinking would be heresy to some who argue that our future lies in linking up with our nearest Big Neighbour under a \u201cconnectivity\u201d agenda. But while remaining grateful to India\u2019s quick support to our requests in times of humanitarian need, we must think clearly of our own national interest in any investment or cooperation partnership. Already Indian foreign investment is capturing Sri Lankan companies and strategic port assets from the Adani joint cooperation in the Colombo Port to the more recent take over of Colombo Dockyard by India\u2019s state-owned Mazagon Dock.\n\nColombo Dockyard which was a regional player and has been building ships and yachts for Europe and earning dollars \u2013 will it be now reduced to repairing dredging vessels and being paid in Indian rupees? The currency exchange scheme with India apparently is still one way, that is Indians can pay Indian rupees for goods and services in Sri Lanka but it seems Sri Lankans cannot pay for goods and services in India with Sri Lankan rupees. Direct currency exchange agreements are useful when reciprocal, avoiding the costly intermediary of the US dollar, an example being the old Asian Currency Union where Sri Lanka is able to settle outstanding balances by the end of the month."
