    "chunk_text": "The current duty-free purchase allowance for arriving passengers is $ 2,000, subject to category-specific quantity limits. All transactions are digitally verified through integration with Sri Lanka Customs systems, ensuring strict regulatory compliance and transparency.\n\nDuty-free shopping eligibility after every overseas trip for Sri Lankan citizens and residents.\n\nTwo visits allowed within the four-day post-arrival purchase period, enabling greater flexibility for travellers\n\nContinued digital verification through Customs systems to ensure compliance with national duty-free allowances\n\nThese regulatory improvements are expected to significantly increase traveller access to duty-free benefits while strengthening Sri Lanka\u2019s position as a modern retail and tourism destination.\n\nCDF Duty Free said it aims to establish Sri Lanka\u2019s first foreign downtown duty-free shopping destination, bringing international retail standards, strong brand partnerships, and competitive pricing to local consumers and travellers.\n\nWith continued Government support, regulatory modernisation, and strong collaboration with industry stakeholders, CDF plans to expand its role in Sri Lanka\u2019s retail and tourism ecosystem while providing travellers with a convenient and premium, but value driven duty-free shopping experience."
