    "chunk_text": "As part of Phase I of the Common Website Platform project, seven Sri Lanka Missions, including Embassy of Sri Lanka in Bucharest, High Commission of Sri Lanka in Mal\u00e9, High Commission of Sri Lanka in New Delhi, Embassy of Sri Lanka in Brasilia, High Commission of Sri Lanka in Wellington, Embassy of Sri Lanka in Hague and Embassy of Sri Lanka in Cairo have been brought under this unified platform. The Common Website Platform project envisages to expand in phases with the objective of bringing all Sri Lanka Missions abroad under one unified and standardised digital platform in the near future.\n\nThe newly launched website and Common Website Platform have been developed with a strong focus on security, reliability, accessibility, and user-friendliness. The launch marks a significant milestone in the digital transformation journey of the Ministry in line with the Government\u2019s Digital Transformation policy and reflects the Government\u2019s broader commitment to strengthening public service delivery through modern, secure, and citizen-centred digital platforms."
  },
