    "md5": "986ed25b94aad6146ac60db2d117cb04",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1349,
    "chunk_text": "Lankan Women Parliamentarians\u2019 Caucus visits India\n\nA 19-member delegation of the Women Parliamentarians\u2019 Caucus of Sri Lanka, led by Sri Lanka Women and Child Affairs Minister Saroja Savithri Paulraj visited India from 10 to 16 May. The delegation comprised of 15 Members of Parliament and four officials of the Parliament of Sri Lanka, including the Secretary General.\n\nThis marks the first-ever visit of the Women Parliamentarians\u2019 Caucus of Sri Lanka to India. It was organised by the Parliamentary Research and Training Institute for Democracies (PRIDE) in collaboration with the External Affairs Ministry Government of India. The visit was in pursuance of the joint vision of Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi and Sri Lanka President Anura Kumara Dissanayake to deepen parliamentary cooperation and strengthen linkages between women leaders of India and Sri Lanka.\n\nDuring the visit, the delegation called on Lok Sabha Speaker Shri Om Birla. Government of India Women and Child Development Minister Smt. Annapurna Devi also received the delegation. They also met Delhi Chief Minister Smt. Rekha Gupta. Discussions centred on fostering collaboration and exchanging best practices in areas of women-led development, gender equality, maternal and child welfare, care economy initiatives, and women\u2019s leadership in politics and governance."
  },
